# {{project_name}}

A Java game built with [raylib](https://www.raylib.com/) (through [jaylib](https://github.com/electronstudio/jaylib)), structured with the Model-View-Controller (MVC) pattern.

## Requirements

A JDK, version {{java_version}} or later. You don't need to install Maven: the included Maven wrapper (`mvnw`) downloads the right version the first time you run it.

On Windows, use `mvnw.cmd` instead of `./mvnw` in the commands below.

## Running

Run directly via Maven (recompiles only changed files):
```
./mvnw compile exec:java
```

Build and run a jar file that includes all dependencies:
```
./mvnw package
java -jar target/{{artifact_id}}-1.0-SNAPSHOT.jar
```

## Testing and formatting

Run the tests:
```
./mvnw test
```

Every Maven build first formats all Java files with [google-java-format](https://github.com/google/google-java-format), so you don't need to format them yourself. If your editor shows a file as changed on disk after a build, reload it.

## Project structure

```
src/main/java/{{package_dir}}/
├── {{main_class}}.java
├── model/
├── view/
└── controller/
src/test/java/{{package_dir}}/
└── model/
```

`{{main_class}}.java` creates the window, wires up the model, view and controller, and runs the game loop. The other packages are described in [MVC rules](#mvc-rules). Put new classes in the package of the part they belong to, and their tests in the matching package under `src/test`.

## MVC rules

Each frame, `{{main_class}}` calls `model.update(dt)` to advance the game, then `view.update()`, which reads input and draws the model.

- **Model** holds the game state and the rules for how it changes. It must not use raylib, so it can be tested without opening a window.
- **View** draws the model and turns raw key presses into events. It reads from the model but never changes it.
- **Controller** registers listeners with the view and decides how to change the model when an event happens. It never draws and never reads raw input.

```
key press ──► View ──event──► Controller ──changes──► Model
               ▲                                        │
               └──────────────── reads ─────────────────┘
```

## NixOS

The included `flake.nix` provides the JDK, Maven, and the graphics libraries that raylib loads at runtime. With [direnv](https://direnv.net/) and nix-direnv, the `.envrc` loads it automatically; otherwise run `nix develop`.
